{
  "about": "CSS Color 4's system colours and its deprecated ones, each row as set on fillStyle: `expected` is what this library reads back, `null` where it refuses the string; `chrome` and `chromePixel` are what Chrome reads back, `null` where it refuses it, and paints on an 8-bit canvas. Read by src/node/utils.rs and tests/suite/system-colors.test.js. A row without `why` reads as Chrome reads it and paints its pixel to one level; a row with `pixel` paints that instead.",
  "source": "Chrome 156.0.8078.49 headless on macOS, light scheme, a 1x1 canvas outside a document, measured 2026-10-28.",
  "why": {
    "float": "A colour derived from a system colour holds its result in floating point and reads back with the figures it holds, where Chrome writes six; tests/assets/cases/css-color-serialisation.json has the rule.",
    "accent": "Chrome 156 refuses `AccentColor` and `AccentColorText`, which CSS Color 4 section 6.2 defines; here they are Chromium's light-scheme control accent, measured from a checked checkbox in the same Chrome, and paint `pixel`. docs/browser-differences.md has the measurement."
  },
  "cases": [
